{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"2":{"eng-name":"Prayer (Kitab Al-Salat)","ara-name":"كتاب الصلاة"}},"section_detail":{"2":{"hadithnumber_first":391,"hadithnumber_last":1160,"arabicnumber_first":391,"arabicnumber_last":1160}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1081,"arabicnumber":1081,"text":"Rapporté par Ibn ‘Umar رضي الله عنه : Quand le Prophète ﷺ a pris du poids, Tamim ad-Dari lui dit : « Veux-tu que je te fabrique une chaire, ô Messager d’Allah, qui supportera ton poids ? » Il répondit : « Oui. » Alors il lui fit une chaire à deux marches","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Hasan"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}],"reference":{"book":2,"hadith":692},"chapter":{"id":223,"ara-name":"باب فِي اتِّخَاذِ الْمِنْبَرِ","eng-name":"On Taking Minbars","isFirstHadith":false}}]}